pipewire: initialize stream variable

Fixes SEGV when controlling the aout (mute, volume) before being started.
Fixes #29211

A film with a picture and no audio track never starts the audio output, and
a press of the volume keys (or the slider) still sets its volume: the
module's state was allocated with malloc and sys->stream was never set, so
VolumeSet and MuteSet took a stream that did not exist and locked the
loop of a garbage pointer (pw_thread_loop_lock(NULL) in the rig; VLC Stereo
+stereo3d20 died with a segmentation fault at the first volume key on a
silent film, ORDER 592).

Origin: upstream, https://github.com/videolan/vlc/commit/30fbe5f3f6be7d0d066c861c6d051d8ccdef5048
Author: Thomas Guillem
Applied-Upstream: VLC master, 30fbe5f3f6 (2025-07-15), after Debian's vlc-plugin-pipewire 3-4 was made
Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code (the context adapted to the copy in the package)

--- a/modules/audio_output/pipewire.c
+++ b/modules/audio_output/pipewire.c
@@ -1014,6 +1014,7 @@
     sys->initial.volume = NAN;
     sys->initial.mute = -1;
     sys->nodes = NULL;
+    sys->stream = NULL;
     sys->settings = NULL;
     sys->clock.force_rate = 0;
     sys->clock.rate = 0;
